{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgasYcmhsf1R94KYcU7n8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've proved `affineLoop_closed` in `Main.lean`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\n```lean\ntheorem affineLoop_closed (n a : Nat) : affineLoop n a + 1 = 2 ^ n * (a + 1) := by\n  induction n generalizing a with\n  | zero => simp [affineLoop]\n  | succ n ih =>\n    rw [affineLoop, ih, Nat.pow_succ, Nat.mul_assoc]\n    congr 1\n```\n\nThe proof uses induction on `n`. The starting value `a` has to be allowed to vary, because each recursive call replaces it with `2a+1`.\n\n- **Base case (`n = 0`):** `affineLoop 0 a` is just `a`, so the goal `a + 1 = 2^0 * (a + 1)` simplifies away.\n- **Step:** Unfolding `affineLoop` once and applying the induction hypothesis gives `2^n * (2a+1+1)`. Rewriting `2^(n+1)` as `2^n * 2` and regrouping the multiplication gives `2^n * (2 * (a+1))`. `congr 1` then reduces the goal to `2a+1+1 = 2*(a+1)`, which it closes on its own.\n\nMy first version ended with an `omega` call. Lean rejected it with \"No goals to be solved\" because `congr 1` had already finished the proof, so I removed it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":457,"cache_read_input_tokens":8606,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":457},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69240668-a167-4c8f-9cc5-549b8be43c76","uuid":"536ba771-9181-4551-840e-86628d440989","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:32:24.473Z","request_id":"req_011CgasYcX5Ns5x3LgXR1RCF"}
